./ R 00643000 00645000 $ 00643100 100                                           
*  WAS SSK R3,R8 / SRL R3,8 / SSK R3,R6 -- THE 2ND HALF        XA0038DK         
*  PAGE'S KEY THEN THE 1ST. AN ESA/390 KEY COVERS THE WHOLE 4  XA0038DK         
*  KB PAGE, SO THE PAIR BECOMES ONE SSKE AND THE SHIFT         XA0038DK         
*  BETWEEN THEM IS NOW THE SELECTION OF WHICH KEY SURVIVES.    XA0038DK         
*  SWPKEY1 IS KEPT, THE FIRST HALF'S. A GUEST THAT SET ITS     XA0038DK         
*  TWO HALVES DIFFERENTLY CANNOT BE REPRESENTED AT ALL --      XA0038DK         
*  THAT IS R-12, GUEST-VISIBLE THROUGH ISKE, AND BELONGS WITH  XA0038DK         
*  M4. RECORDED HERE SO THE CHOICE IS NOT MISTAKEN FOR AN      XA0038DK         
*  EQUIVALENCE. R8 STILL CARRIES THE 2ND-HALF ADDRESS FROM     XA0038DK         
*  00640000 AND IS NOW UNUSED; THE LA IS LEFT ALONE SO NO      XA0038DK         
*  OTHER REGISTER STATE CHANGES. I-177.                        XA0038DK         
         SRL   R3,8           SWPKEY1, THE FIRST HALF'S KEY    XA0038DK         
         SSKE  R3,R6          ONE KEY FOR THE WHOLE PAGE       XA0038DK         
./ R 00939000 00940000 $ 00939100 100                                           
*  WAS SSK R6,R7 / SSK R6,R5 -- FIRST 2K THEN SECOND 2K, BOTH  XA0038DK         
*  WITH THE KEY ZEROED BY SR R6,R6 AT 00937000. ONE KEY, ONE   XA0038DK         
*  INSTRUCTION, AND NOTHING IS LOST BECAUSE BOTH HALVES WERE   XA0038DK         
*  ALREADY BEING SET THE SAME. I-177.                          XA0038DK         
         SSKE  R6,R7          ZERO KEY, WHOLE 4 KB PAGE        XA0038DK         
